# Standardized Logging

## Single entry point

- All backend logs go through `createLogger` from `@app/shared` — **including API Gateway access logs**.
- Nest runtime logs use `NestStandardLogger` (wraps `createLogger`). Never `console.*` in handlers/use-cases/adapters.
- Prefer `createApplicationLogger(domain, operation)` (or `logger.child({ layer, operation })`) in use-cases.

```typescript
import {
  createLogger,
  createApplicationLogger,
  logHttpRequest,
  NestStandardLogger,
} from '@app/shared';

const logger = createLogger('transactions');
logger.info('transaction.created', { transactionId });

const payLog = createApplicationLogger('transactions', 'pay_transaction');
payLog.info('pay.outcome', { paymentStatus: 'APPROVED' });

// API access (same JSON envelope)
logHttpRequest({ method, path, statusCode, durationMs, correlationId, targetService });
```

## Standard shape

Every line is one JSON object:

`timestamp`, `level`, `service`, `message`, `stage`, optional `functionName` / `runtime`, optional `correlationId` / `requestId`, optional `domain` / `layer` / `operation`, optional `data` (redacted).

| Kind | `service` | `layer` | `message` |
|---|---|---|---|
| Domain / Lambda | microservice name | `infrastructure` / `adapter` / … | event key e.g. `lambda.cold_start` |
| Application use-case | domain name | `application` | e.g. `pay.outcome` |
| HTTP access (API) | `api-gateway` | `http` | `http.request` |

HTTP `data` includes: `channel: "http"`, `method`, `path`, `route` (normalized), `statusCode`, `statusClass`, `durationMs`, `targetService`, `coldStart`, optional `userAgent` / `contentLength`.

HTTP access also emits **EMF** custom metrics under namespace `Checkout/API` (see `docs/observability.md`).

## Wiring

- Each Nest app: `AccessLogMiddleware(serviceName)` on all routes + `NestStandardLogger` in `NestFactory.create`.
- Propagate `x-correlation-id` on every response.
- Lambda handlers: pass `requestId: context.awsRequestId` into `createLogger` meta.
- CloudWatch dashboards / alarms / IAM viewer: `infra/observability-resources.cjs` via Serverless.
